<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cato the Elder</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cato the Elder was a Roman statesman and writer of the second century BCE, famous for his conservatism and moral severity. He is remembered for ending his speeches with the declaration that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> must be destroyed. His campaigning helped bring about the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-punic-war">Third Punic War</a>, which ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punic-empire">Punic Empire</a> in 146 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cato-the-elder.jpg" alt="Cato the Elder" width="302" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Patrizio_Torlonia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
